body:
Greg's direction on the crate split, 2026-11-03, relayed verbatim by Engram::Asistant in TermAl mailbox 588693a8.

#121 (06:35Z): „Ok. To bedzie następna rzecz po poprawkach.” Splitting the backend into smaller Rust crates is the NEXT work stream, once the current fix queue has landed.

#125 (06:41Z), the GOAL: „Bardziej chodzi nie o zysk kompilacji a testy. Crate miały by unit testy. Termal main unit testy i integration tests(cięższe). Można by je uruchamiać równolegle.” The primary objective is test structure and parallel execution, not compile time. The target shape:
- per-crate unit tests;
- main-crate unit tests kept separate from the heavier integration tests;
- isolation boundaries for shared resources;
- a safe parallel-run plan that runs no test twice and still runs every needed integration test;
- measured wall-clock time.

How it is being handled:
- The spike w-ae109290885c (Termal::Architect2) produces the executable plan. Fable2's preliminary draft went to Greg in #124, labelled as a hypothesis.
- The team proceeds autonomously after the fix queue.
